            <p>Bruit Assessment Sites. The 3 most frequent sites to assess for a bruit: (1) proximal to the upstroke of cardiac murmurs; (2) at the angle of the mandible and the carotid bifurcation; and (3) over the orbit to assess for carotid-cavernous fistula. Contributed by R Benjamin, MD, MPH</p>
